Offering is good for your relation to your god. If you think he likes you a lot
try #pray-ing at the altar. Depending on what your god really thinks about you
you might get a goodie. Take care to #offer some more and wait several hundred
turns before trying again. If you are in optimal relation with your god, have
not prayed for some time and have good luck, you can get objects by #offer-ing
too.

About "Nothing happens": Your god doesn't like old meat (value of an offer is
calculated from age and difficulty to kill, thus orcs are not very interesting
to your god once you reached a higher level). However even newt corpses are
accepted (though not very influencing) if they are fresh enough, while even a
black dragon corpse will be rejected ("Nothing happens") if it's too old (it may
still be edible by you!). Btw. everything older than 50 time steps is "too old".



